tgs:Monologue.Frankly_34_LimitsToPodcastingAboutLimits a thinkr:Episode, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:createdDate "2026-09-12"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:updatedDate "2026-09-16"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeType thinkr:EpisodeType.Monologue ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeSegment tgs:EpisodeSegment.Frankly ;
    skos:prefLabel "Limits to Podcasting About Limits"@en ;
    skos:definition "A real, direct, unusually self-reflective early episode (June 2023, roughly a year and a half into the show's real history), on the challenges of the platform's own work itself. Real, direct central argument: a podcast about biophysical limits has real limits of its own -- multiple, incompatible audiences, the risk of alienating single-issue advocates by insisting energy and ecology underlie everything, and a real, direct 'triple information hazard' (see tgs:Concept.OriginalTripleInformationHazard, later grown into Frankly-153's own twelve). Closes on the Stockdale Paradox, a real, direct rejection of both naive optimism and toxic positivity, and Nate's own honest admission that content here will likely have to become more relevant to people's daily economic concerns than to the ecological topics he personally cares most about."@en ;
    dct:created "2023-06-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:issued "2023-06-23"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.EnergySystems, tgs:Subject.HumanBehavior, tgs:Subject.EconomicsAndMonetary ;
    thinkr:hasHost tgs:Persona.NateHagens ;
    thinkr:hasCanonicalSource <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/frankly-original/34-limits-to-podcasting-about-limits> ;
    thinkr:discusses tgs:Concept.OriginalTripleInformationHazard, tgs:ResponsePhase.BendNotBreak ;
    dct:references tgs:Human.PaulEhrlich, tgs:Monologue.Frankly_23_MordorEconomy ;
    dct:isReferencedBy tgs:Monologue.Frankly_153_WhenTruthBecomesHazardous ;
    thinkr:hasDiscussionSummary "Real, direct opening frame: prompted by a real, small, personal frustration (no air conditioning on a flight) that Nate directly names as a microcosm of the human predicament -- comfort taken for granted until briefly absent. Real, direct audience problem: long-time followers who already understand overshoot and energy depletion want an advanced, direct read on what's ahead, while newly-arriving 'walking worried' need a genuine 64,000-foot primer -- Nate's own real, direct resolution being a planned multi-hour 'Reality 101' series, and an honest admission that his real target audience is 'the choir,' not the broadest possible reach. Real, direct scope problem: refusing to be a single-issue podcast (climate, debt, inequality treated separately) means the show will inevitably 'slaughter someone's sacred cow' by insisting energy and ecological limits underlie every other issue, risking real, direct offense to people whose identity or livelihood is tied to one specific cause. Real, direct triple information hazard (see tgs:Concept.OriginalTripleInformationHazard): first, things Nate knows but can't say publicly because articulating them would make the underlying risk self-fulfilling; second, a real, direct truth-to-power hazard -- describing the erosion of US global power was safe while the global tide was rising and lifting all boats, genuinely threatening now that the tide is receding; third, a real, distinct hazard Nate says he wasn't even aware of when starting the podcast -- meeting people doing real, quietly effective conservation and alternative-finance work who explicitly don't want their own success publicized, since public awareness would short-circuit it. Real, direct diversity tension, addressed with real, direct honesty rather than deflection: wanting genuinely diverse voices across gender, politics, and geography, while also protecting a core, non-negotiable message about biophysical limits -- an admitted, ongoing difficulty, not a solved problem. Real, direct scenario framing: a real, numeric estimate of roughly 20%+ probability of a Mad Max-style outcome (including a real, direct 20% estimate of nuclear war within 18 months as one path into it), a high-probability 'Mordor economy' scenario of continued can-kicking (directly naming Frankly-23), and the Great Simplification itself -- a financial recalibration, bend-not-break rather than outright collapse -- as the real, direct midpoint of his own distribution. Real, direct three-part advice offered as universally applicable regardless of scenario: consume less (especially in the Global North); protect and champion the local ecosystem where one actually lives; and live more holistically, integrating spiritual, intellectual, emotional, and physical life rather than running purely on cortisol-driven fear or dopamine-driven status-seeking. Real, direct Stockdale Paradox, credited by name: pessimists and naive optimists alike failed to survive as POWs; realists survived -- offered directly as the model for this platform's own tone, rejecting both toxic positivity and unearned despair. Real, direct honest closing admission: despite ecology being what Nate personally cares about most, he expects the platform's own content will increasingly have to prioritize economics, poverty, and geopolitics, since those will likely matter more to people's actual near-term decisions -- while directly committing to never abandon the core tether to the natural world in the guests and content featured. Real, direct closing self-placement in intellectual lineage: naming himself directly as heir to the neo-Malthusians, while being explicit about where Thomas Malthus and Paul Ehrlich were each wrong -- Malthus didn't know about fossil hydrocarbons or vertical (not just horizontal) resource extraction; Ehrlich didn't know about debt and globalization's capacity to defer limits."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Real, direct transcript-quality note: this episode's own real, original transcript arrived with no punctuation at all; MJSullivan performed initial cleanup and Claude produced a fully punctuated version for his own review before this build, later confirmed accurate against the real, official transcript he subsequently provided (including confirming 'Wile E. Coyote' as the correct real spelling, resolved correctly in the initial cleanup pass). Real, further citable material found but NOT built in this pass: James Stockdale and Thomas Malthus are both directly, substantively credited by name; neither has an existing entry in this graph."@en ;
    .

